From 9bcc6c053b53a2dfe7e53c854c8c9856ad4ef2e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:02:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] FFmpeg: the CUDA converter frees its OpenGL textures on any
 thread

CUDAGLTextureConverter holds GL textures registered with CUDA, and its destructor
made the QRhi's OpenGL context current to delete them. The converter is destroyed
by whoever lets go the last reference to the decoder's frames context
(HwFrameContextData, through av_buffer_unref), and that is not always the
thread of the context: a player that opens another file closes the decoder on
the GUI thread (QMediaPlayer::setSource, QFFmpeg::PlaybackEngine's destructor,
avcodec_free_context), while the scene graph's render thread owns the context.
QOpenGLContext::makeCurrent() then aborts the process: "Cannot make
QOpenGLContext current in a different thread". Which thread drops the last
reference depends on how long the render thread keeps its last frame, so it
happens at some source changes and not at others.

The converter now makes the context current only on the context's own thread.
On another thread it gives its planes, the textures and their CUDA registrations,
to the share group of the context (QOpenGLSharedResource), which frees them when
one of its contexts is next made current, as Qt does for its own textures. CUDA
refuses to unregister the resource of a texture without the texture's context
current (cuGraphicsUnregisterResource returns CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_GRAPHICS_CONTEXT,
219, and the result was never looked at), so the unregistering waits for the
right thread too, and the plane keeps a reference to the decoder's device so that
the CUDA context is still there then. A failed unregistration is now said.

tst_qffmpegcudatextureconverter releases the frames context of a CUDA frame on
the context's thread and on another thread, checks that the textures are gone
after the context is next made current and that no unregistration failed. It
skips without an NVIDIA GPU. Before the change the second case aborts with the
message above.

Upstream: the converter is Tim Blechmann's c57f4af5ab in dev (carried as the
patch before this one); dev's file has the same destructor and no later change
(searched 2026-11-10: the file's history, dev's commits since 2026-09-10,
QTBUG-129994, which is the same abort for another path and was fixed by the QRhi
refactoring of 6.8.2).

